## How to add text to the input of a bootstrap select?

To add text to the input of a bootstrap select, you can use the `title` attribute of the `select` element. For example, if you want to add the text "Select an option" to the input, you can do so as follows:

HTML:

`<select class="form-control" title="Select an option">`

JavaScript (if using Bootstrap select plugin):

```language-javascript
$('#select').selectpicker({
    title: 'Select an option'
});
```

This will add the text "Select an option" to the input of the bootstrap select when it is rendered.

## What is the HTML select input type?

The HTML select input type is used to create a drop-down list in a form. It allows users to select one or more options from a predefined list. The select element is commonly used in forms for things like choosing a country, selecting a size, or picking a date range. The selected value can be submitted along with the rest of the form data when the form is submitted.

## How to add text to a bootstrap select dropdown?

To add text to a bootstrap select dropdown, you can simply add an option with a value of an empty string and include the desired text in the option's label. Here is an example:

```html
<select class="form-control" id="myDropdown">
    <option value="">Choose an option</option>
    <option value="option1">Option 1</option>
    <option value="option2">Option 2</option>
    <option value="option3">Option 3</option>
</select>
```

